verses.text:
The name of the first \add is\add* Pison: that \add is\add*
it which compasseth the whole land of Havilah, where \add there is\add*
gold;

And the \nd LORD\nd* God caused a deep sleep to fall upon
Adam, and he slept: and he took one of his ribs, and closed up the
flesh instead thereof;

Of fowls also of the air by sevens, the male and the female;
to keep seed alive upon the face of all the earth.\f + \fr 7.3  \ft by sevens: Heb. seven
seven\f*

In the selfsame day entered Noah, and Shem, and Ham, and Japheth,
the sons of Noah, and Noah’s wife, and the three wives of his sons
with them, into the ark;

And God remembered Noah, and every living thing, and all the
cattle that \add was\add* with him in the ark: and God made a wind
to pass over the earth, and the waters asswaged;

And he went on his journeys from the south even to Beth-el,
unto the place where his tent had been at the beginning, between
Beth-el and Hai;

And it came to pass in the days of Amraphel king of Shinar,
Arioch king of Ellasar, Chedorlaomer king of Elam, and Tidal king
of nations;

With Chedorlaomer the king of Elam, and with Tidal king of
nations, and Amraphel king of Shinar, and Arioch king of Ellasar;
four kings with five.

And there came one that had escaped, and told Abram the Hebrew;
for he dwelt in the plain of Mamre the Amorite, brother of Eshcol,
and brother of Aner: and these \add were\add* confederate with Abram.\f + \fr 14.13 
\ft plain: Heb. plains\f*

And he said unto Abram, Know of a surety that thy seed shall be a
stranger in a land \add that is\add* not theirs, and shall serve
them; and they shall afflict them four hundred years;

And as for Ishmael, I have heard thee: Behold, I have blessed
him, and will make him fruitful, and will multiply him exceedingly;
twelve princes shall he beget, and I will make him a great nation.

And there came two angels to Sodom at even; and Lot sat in the
gate of Sodom: and Lot seeing \add them\add* rose up to meet them; and he
bowed himself with his face toward the ground;

And Abraham took the wood of the burnt offering, and laid \add it\add*
upon Isaac his son; and he took the fire in his hand, and a knife;
and they went both of them together.

And it came to pass after these things, that it was told
Abraham, saying, Behold, Milcah, she hath also born children unto thy
brother Nahor;

Behold, I stand by the well of water; and it shall come to pass, that when the
virgin cometh forth to draw \add water\add*, and I say to her, Give
me, I pray thee, a little water of thy pitcher to drink;

And his sons Isaac and Ishmael buried him in the cave of Machpelah,
in the field of Ephron the son of Zohar the Hittite, which \add is\add*
before Mamre;

Sojourn in this land, and I will be with thee, and will bless
thee; for unto thee, and unto thy seed, I will give all these countries,
and I will perform the oath which I sware unto Abraham thy father;

And I will make thy seed to multiply as the stars of heaven,
and will give unto thy seed all these countries; and in thy seed
shall all the nations of the earth be blessed;

And Jacob said unto his father, I \add am\add* Esau thy firstborn;
I have done according as thou badest me: arise, I pray thee, sit
and eat of my venison, that thy soul may bless me.

And by thy sword shalt thou live, and shalt serve thy brother;
and it shall come to pass when thou shalt have the dominion, that thou shalt
break his yoke from off thy neck.

If thou shalt afflict my daughters, or if thou shalt take
\add other\add* wives beside my daughters, no man \add is\add* with us;
see, God \add is\add* witness betwixt me and thee.

Then Jacob was greatly afraid and distressed: and he divided
the people that \add was\add* with him, and the flocks, and herds,
and the camels, into two bands;

And God said unto him, I \add am\add* God Almighty: be fruitful
and multiply; a nation and a company of nations shall be of thee, and
kings shall come out of thy loins;

Esau took his wives of the daughters of Canaan; Adah the daughter
of Elon the Hittite, and Aholibamah the daughter of Anah the daughter
of Zibeon the Hivite;

For their riches were more than that they might dwell together;
and the land wherein they were strangers could not bear them because
of their cattle.

And these \add are\add* the sons of Aholibamah Esau’s wife;
duke Jeush, duke Jaalam, duke Korah: these \add were\add* the dukes
\add that came\add* of Aholibamah the daughter of Anah, Esau’s wife.

But he refused, and said unto his master’s wife, Behold, my
master wotteth not what \add is\add* with me in the house, and he hath
committed all that he hath to my hand;

And there shall arise after them seven years of famine; and all the
plenty shall be forgotten in the land of Egypt; and the famine shall
consume the land;

Now therefore when I come to thy servant my father, and the
lad \add be\add* not with us; seeing that his life is bound up in the lad’s
life;

And Joseph said unto his brethren, and unto his father’s house,
I will go up, and shew Pharaoh, and say unto him, My brethren, and my
father’s house, which \add were\add* in the land of Canaan, are come unto me;

Cursed \add be\add* their anger, for \add it was\add* fierce;
and their wrath, for it was cruel: I will divide them in Jacob, and
scatter them in Israel.

All these \add are\add* the twelve tribes of Israel: and this
\add is it\add* that their father spake unto them, and blessed them;
every one according to his blessing he blessed them.

And the \nd LORD\nd* said, I have surely seen the affliction
of my people which \add are\add* in Egypt, and have heard their cry
by reason of their taskmasters; for I know their sorrows;

And Moses and Aaron did so, as the \nd LORD\nd* commanded;
and he lifted up the rod, and smote the waters that \add were\add*
in the river, in the sight of Pharaoh, and in the sight of his servants;
and all the waters that \add were\add* in the river were turned to
blood.

And they took ashes of the furnace, and stood before Pharaoh;
and Moses sprinkled it up toward heaven; and it became a boil breaking
forth \add with\add* blains upon man, and upon beast.

And this day shall be unto you for a memorial; and ye shall
keep it a feast to the \nd LORD\nd* throughout your generations;
ye shall keep it a feast by an ordinance for ever.

And the children of Israel did according to the word of Moses;
and they borrowed of the Egyptians jewels of silver, and jewels of
gold, and raiment:

The \nd LORD\nd* \add is\add* my strength and song, and he is become my
salvation: he \add is\add* my God, and I will prepare him an habitation;
my father’s God, and I will exalt him.

And Moses and Aaron said unto all the children of Israel, At
even, then ye shall know that the \nd LORD\nd* hath brought you out
from the land of Egypt:

When Jethro, the priest of Midian, Moses’ father in law, heard
of all that God had done for Moses, and for Israel his people, \add and\add*
that the \nd LORD\nd* had brought Israel out of Egypt;

And Moses went out to meet his father in law, and did obeisance,
and kissed him; and they asked each other of \add their\add* welfare;
and they came into the tent.\f + \fr 18.7  \ft welfare: Heb. peace\f*

And Moses went up unto God, and the \nd LORD\nd* called unto him out of the
mountain, saying, Thus shalt thou say to the house of Jacob, and
tell the children of Israel;

Or if it be known that the ox hath used to push in time past,
and his owner hath not kept him in; he shall surely pay ox for ox;
and the dead shall be his own.

If the sun be risen upon him, \add there shall be\add* blood
\add shed\add* for him; \add for\add* he should make full restitution;
if he have nothing, then he shall be sold for his theft.

And this \add is\add* the offering which ye shall take of them;
gold, and silver, and brass,\f + \fr 25.3  \ft offering: or, heave
offering\f*

And I, behold, I have given with him Aholiab, the son of Ahisamach,
of the tribe of Dan: and in the hearts of all that are wise hearted
I have put wisdom, that they may make all that I have commanded thee;

And it shall come to pass, while my glory passeth by, that I will
put thee in a clift of the rock, and will cover thee with my hand
while I pass by:

Lest thou make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land,
and they go a whoring after their gods, and do sacrifice unto their
gods, and \add one\add* call thee, and thou eat of his sacrifice;

Thou shalt not offer the blood of my sacrifice with leaven;
neither shall the sacrifice of the feast of the passover be left
unto the morning.

And Moses said unto the children of Israel, See, the \nd LORD\nd*
hath called by name Bezaleel the son of Uri, the son of Hur, of the
tribe of Judah;

And forty sockets of silver he made under the twenty boards;
two sockets under one board for his two tenons, and two sockets under
another board for his two tenons.

And he made thereunto four pillars \add of\add* shittim \add wood\add*,
and overlaid them with gold: their hooks \add were of\add* gold;
and he cast for them four sockets of silver.

And they made bells \add of\add* pure gold, and put the bells
between the pomegranates upon the hem of the robe, round about between
the pomegranates;

And the priest of his sons that is anointed in his stead shall
offer it: \add it is\add* a statute for ever unto the \nd LORD\nd*;
it shall be wholly burnt.

This \add is\add* the law of the burnt offering, of the meat
offering, and of the sin offering, and of the trespass offering,
and of the consecrations, and of the sacrifice of the peace offerings;

Take Aaron and his sons with him, and the garments, and the
anointing oil, and a bullock for the sin offering, and two rams,
and a basket of unleavened bread;

And he put the mitre upon his head; also upon the mitre, \add even\add*
upon his forefront, did he put the golden plate, the holy crown;
as the \nd LORD\nd* commanded Moses.

And unto the children of Israel thou shalt speak, saying, Take
ye a kid of the goats for a sin offering; and a calf and a lamb,
\add both\add* of the first year, without blemish, for a burnt offering;

Yet these may ye eat of every flying creeping thing that goeth upon
\add all\add* four, which have legs above their feet, to leap withal
upon the earth;

And if a leprosy break out abroad in the skin, and the leprosy
cover all the skin of \add him that hath\add* the plague from his
head even to his foot, wheresoever the priest looketh;

And in the seventh day the priest shall look on the plague: and, behold,
\add if\add* the scall spread not, and there be in it no yellow hair,
and the scall \add be\add* not in sight deeper than the skin;

And if the priest shall look, and, behold, the plague be not
spread in the garment, either in the warp, or in the woof, or in any
thing of skin;

And the priest shall go forth out of the camp; and the priest
shall look, and, behold, \add if\add* the plague of leprosy be healed
in the leper;

When ye be come into the land of Canaan, which I give to you for a
possession, and I put the plague of leprosy in a house of the land
of your possession;

And the priest shall come again the seventh day, and shall
look: and, behold, \add if\add* the plague be spread in the walls
of the house;

And if the plague come again, and break out in the house,
after that he hath taken away the stones, and after he hath scraped
the house, and after it is plaistered;

And if he that hath the issue spit upon him that is clean;
then he shall wash his clothes, and bathe \add himself\add* in water,
and be unclean until the even.

Thus shall ye separate the children of Israel from their uncleanness;
that they die not in their uncleanness, when they defile my tabernacle that
\add is\add* among them.

Do not prostitute thy daughter, to cause her to be a whore;
lest the land fall to whoredom, and the land become full of wickedness.\f + \fr 19.29 
\ft prostitute: Heb. profane\f*

And I will set my face against that man, and will cut him off
from among his people; because he hath given of his seed unto Molech,
to defile my sanctuary, and to profane my holy name.

And the man that lieth with his father’s wife hath uncovered
his father’s nakedness: both of them shall surely be put to death;
their blood \add shall be\add* upon them.

And if a woman approach unto any beast, and lie down thereto, thou shalt
kill the woman, and the beast: they shall surely be put to death;
their blood \add shall be\add* upon them.

And the \nd LORD\nd* said unto Moses, Speak unto the priests
the sons of Aaron, and say unto them, There shall none be defiled
for the dead among his people:

They shall not take a wife \add that is\add* a whore, or profane;
neither shall they take a woman put away from her husband: for he
\add is\add* holy unto his God.

I \add am\add* the \nd LORD\nd* your God, which brought you
forth out of the land of Egypt, that ye should not be their bondmen;
and I have broken the bands of your yoke, and made you go upright.

If they shall confess their iniquity, and the iniquity of their
fathers, with their trespass which they trespassed against me, and that also they have
walked contrary unto me;

And if \add a man\add* sanctify unto the \nd LORD\nd* a field
which he hath bought, which \add is\add* not of the fields of his
possession;

Take ye the sum of all the congregation of the children of
Israel, after their families, by the house of their fathers, with the
number of \add their\add* names, every male by their polls;

So were all those that were numbered of the children of Israel,
by the house of their fathers, from twenty years old and upward,
all that were able to go forth to war in Israel;

And I, behold, I have taken the Levites from among the children
of Israel instead of all the firstborn that openeth the matrix among the
children of Israel: therefore the Levites shall be mine;

Take the Levites instead of all the firstborn among the children
of Israel, and the cattle of the Levites instead of their cattle;
and the Levites shall be mine: I \add am\add* the \nd LORD\nd*.

And for those that are to be redeemed of the two hundred and threescore and
thirteen of the firstborn of the children of Israel, which are more
than the Levites;

Of the firstborn of the children of Israel took he the money;
a thousand three hundred and threescore and five \add shekels\add*,
after the shekel of the sanctuary:

Speak unto the children of Israel, When a man or woman shall
commit any sin that men commit, to do a trespass against the \nd LORD\nd*,
and that person be guilty;

And the priest shall take holy water in an earthen vessel;
and of the dust that is in the floor of the tabernacle the priest
shall take, and put \add it\add* into the water:

And the Levites were purified, and they washed their clothes;
and Aaron offered them \add as\add* an offering before the \nd LORD\nd*;
and Aaron made an atonement for them to cleanse them.

And the sons of Aaron, the priests, shall blow with the trumpets;
and they shall be to you for an ordinance for ever throughout your
generations.

And it came to pass, when the ark set forward, that Moses
said, Rise up, \nd LORD\nd*, and let thine enemies be scattered;
and let them that hate thee flee before thee.

And see the land, what it \add is;\add* and the people that
dwelleth therein, whether they \add be\add* strong or weak, few or
many;

And what the land \add is\add* that they dwell in, whether it
\add be\add* good or bad; and what cities \add they be\add* that they
dwell in, whether in tents, or in strong holds;

Because all those men which have seen my glory, and my miracles,
which I did in Egypt and in the wilderness, and have tempted me now these
ten times, and have not hearkened to my voice;

But my servant Caleb, because he had another spirit with him, and hath
followed me fully, him will I bring into the land whereinto he went;
and his seed shall possess it.

Speak unto Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest, that he take
up the censers out of the burning, and scatter thou the fire yonder;
for they are hallowed.

And when Phinehas, the son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron the
priest, saw \add it\add*, he rose up from among the congregation,
and took a javelin in his hand;

Take the sum of all the congregation of the children of Israel,
from twenty years old and upward, throughout their fathers’ house,
all that are able to go to war in Israel.

Reuben, the eldest son of Israel: the children of Reuben;
Hanoch, \add of whom cometh\add* the family of the Hanochites: of
Pallu, the family of the Palluites:

The daughters of Zelophehad speak right: thou shalt surely
give them a possession of an inheritance among their father’s brethren;
and thou shalt cause the inheritance of their father to pass unto them.

And the \nd LORD\nd* said unto Moses, Take thee Joshua the
son of Nun, a man in whom \add is\add* the spirit, and lay thine
hand upon him;

And in the beginnings of your months ye shall offer a burnt
offering unto the \nd LORD\nd*; two young bullocks, and one ram,
seven lambs of the first year without spot;

And three tenth deals of flour \add for\add* a meat offering,
mingled with oil, for one bullock; and two tenth deals of flour \add for\add*
a meat offering, mingled with oil, for one ram;

And their meat offering \add shall be of\add* flour mingled
 with oil: three tenth deals shall ye offer for a bullock, and two
tenth deals for a ram;

But ye shall offer the burnt offering for a sweet savour unto the
\nd LORD\nd*; two young bullocks, one ram, seven lambs of the first
year;

And Eleazar the priest said unto the men of war which went
to the battle, This \add is\add* the ordinance of the law which the
\nd LORD\nd* commanded Moses;

And the asses \add were\add* thirty thousand and five hundred;
of which the \nd LORD’s\nd* tribute \add was\add* threescore and
one.

And they shall be unto you cities for refuge from the avenger;
that the manslayer die not, until he stand before the congregation
in judgment.

The \nd LORD\nd* your God which goeth before you, he shall
fight for you, according to all that he did for you in Egypt before your
eyes;

Thou shalt sell me meat for money, that I may eat; and give
me water for money, that I may drink: only I will pass through on my
feet;

And we took at that time out of the hand of the two kings of the
Amorites the land that \add was\add* on this side Jordan, from the
river of Arnon unto mount Hermon;

And unto the Reubenites and unto the Gadites I gave from Gilead
even unto the river Arnon half the valley, and the border even unto the
river Jabbok, \add which is\add* the border of the children of Ammon;

But your wives, and your little ones, and your cattle, (\add for\add*
I know that ye have much cattle,) shall abide in your cities which I have
given you;

Only take heed to thyself, and keep thy soul diligently, lest thou
forget the things which thine eyes have seen, and lest they depart
from thy heart all the days of thy life: but teach them thy sons,
and thy sons’ sons;

And because he loved thy fathers, therefore he chose their
seed after them, and brought thee out in his sight with his mighty
power out of Egypt;

And they possessed his land, and the land of Og king of Bashan,
two kings of the Amorites, which \add were\add* on this side Jordan
toward the sunrising;

Know therefore that the \nd LORD\nd* thy God, he \add is\add*
God, the faithful God, which keepeth covenant and mercy with them that
love him and keep his commandments to a thousand generations;

Thou shalt not be afraid of them: \add but\add* shalt well
remember what the \nd LORD\nd* thy God did unto Pharaoh, and unto all
Egypt;

For the \nd LORD\nd* thy God bringeth thee into a good land,
a land of brooks of water, of fountains and depths that spring out
of valleys and hills;

Then thine heart be lifted up, and thou forget the \nd LORD\nd*
thy God, which brought thee forth out of the land of Egypt, from the
house of bondage;

Who fed thee in the wilderness with manna, which thy fathers
knew not, that he might humble thee, and that he might prove thee, to do thee
good at thy latter end;

Thy fathers went down into Egypt with threescore and ten persons;
and now the \nd LORD\nd* thy God hath made thee as the stars of heaven
for multitude.

Therefore shall ye keep all the commandments which I command
you this day, that ye may be strong, and go in and possess the land,
whither ye go to possess it;

For if ye shall diligently keep all these commandments which I
command you, to do them, to love the \nd LORD\nd* your God, to walk
in all his ways, and to cleave unto him;

And the sign or the wonder come to pass, whereof he spake unto thee,
saying, Let us go after other gods, which thou hast not known, and let us
serve them;

\add Namely\add*, of the gods of the people which \add are\add*
round about you, nigh unto thee, or far off from thee, from the \add one\add*
end of the earth even unto the \add other\add* end of the earth;

Then shalt thou enquire, and make search, and ask diligently; and, behold,
\add if it be\add* truth, \add and\add* the thing certain, \add that\add*
such abomination is wrought among you;

For the \nd LORD\nd* thy God blesseth thee, as he promised
thee: and thou shalt lend unto many nations, but thou shalt not borrow;
and thou shalt reign over many nations, but they shall not reign over thee.

And if a Levite come from any of thy gates out of all Israel,
where he sojourned, and come with all the desire of his mind unto the
place which the \nd LORD\nd* shall choose;

The \nd LORD\nd* thy God will raise up unto thee a Prophet
from the midst of thee, of thy brethren, like unto me; unto him ye shall
hearken;

And if the \nd LORD\nd* thy God enlarge thy coast, as he hath
sworn unto thy fathers, and give thee all the land which he promised
to give unto thy fathers;

Then both the men, between whom the controversy \add is\add*,
shall stand before the \nd LORD\nd*, before the priests and the judges,
which shall be in those days;

And the judges shall make diligent inquisition: and, behold,
\add if\add* the witness \add be\add* a false witness, \add and\add*
hath testified falsely against his brother;

And they shall say unto the elders of his city, This our son
\add is\add* stubborn and rebellious, he will not obey our voice;
\add he is\add* a glutton, and a drunkard.

Then the man that lay with her shall give unto the damsel’s
father fifty \add shekels\add* of silver, and she shall be his wife;
because he hath humbled her, he may not put her away all his days.

And it shall be, when thou \add art\add* come in unto the land
which the \nd LORD\nd* thy God giveth  thee \add for\add* an inheritance,
and possessest it, and dwellest therein;

And the \nd LORD\nd* hath avouched thee this day to be his
peculiar people, as he hath promised thee, and that \add thou\add*
shouldest keep all his commandments;

Cursed \add be\add* he that lieth with his father’s wife;
because he uncovereth his father’s skirt. And all the people shall
say, Amen.

If thou wilt not observe to do all the words of this law that are
written in this book, that thou mayest fear this glorious and fearful
name, THE \nd LORD\nd* THY GOD;

And Moses called unto all Israel, and said unto them, Ye have
seen all that the \nd LORD\nd* did before your eyes in the land of
Egypt unto Pharaoh, and unto all his servants, and unto all his land;

And shalt return unto the \nd LORD\nd* thy God, and shalt obey
his voice according to all that I command thee this day, thou and thy
children, with all thine heart, and with all thy soul;

For I know thy rebellion, and thy stiff neck: behold, while I am yet
alive with you this day, ye have been rebellious against the \nd LORD\nd*;
and how much more after my death?

He found him in a desert land, and in the waste howling wilderness;
he led him about, he instructed him, he kept him as the apple of his
eye.\f + \fr 32.10  \ft led: or, compassed\f*

He made him ride on the high places of the earth, that he might
eat the increase of the fields; and he made him to suck honey out of the
rock, and oil out of the flinty rock;

And he said, I will hide my face from them, I will see what their
end \add shall be:\add* for they \add are\add* a very froward generation,
children in whom \add is\add* no faith.

And of Levi he said, \add Let\add* thy Thummim and thy Urim
\add be\add* with thy holy one, whom thou didst prove at Massah,
\add and with\add* whom thou didst strive at the waters of Meribah;

And Joshua the son of Nun was full of the spirit of wisdom;
for Moses had laid his hands upon him: and the children of Israel
hearkened  unto him, and did as the \nd LORD\nd* commanded Moses.

Have not I commanded thee? Be strong and of a good courage;
be not afraid, neither be thou dismayed: for the \nd LORD\nd* thy
God \add is\add* with thee whithersoever thou goest.

And it came to pass, when the people removed from their tents,
to pass over Jordan, and the priests bearing the ark of the covenant
before the people;

And he commanded them, saying, Behold, ye shall lie in wait
against the city, \add even\add* behind the city: go not very far
from the city, but be ye all ready:

They did work wilily, and went and made as if they had been
ambassadors, and took old sacks upon their asses, and wine bottles,
old, and rent, and bound up;

Now it came to pass, when Adoni-zedek king of Jerusalem had
heard how Joshua had taken Ai, and had utterly destroyed it; as he had
done to Jericho and her king, so he had done to Ai and her king;
and how the inhabitants of Gibeon had made peace with Israel, and were
among them;

So Joshua took all that land, the hills, and all the south
country, and all the land of Goshen, and the valley, and the plain,
and the mountain of Israel, and the valley of the same;

And these \add are\add* the kings of the country which Joshua
and the children of Israel smote on this side Jordan on the west,
from Baal-gad in the valley of Lebanon even unto the mount Halak,
that goeth up to Seir; which Joshua gave unto the tribes of Israel
\add for\add* a possession according to their divisions;

With whom the Reubenites and the Gadites have received their
inheritance, which Moses gave them, beyond Jordan eastward, \add even\add*
as Moses the servant of the \nd LORD\nd* gave them;

From Aroer, that \add is\add* upon the bank of the river Arnon,
and the city that \add is\add* in the midst of the river, and all the
plain of Medeba unto Dibon;

And their coast was from Aroer, that \add is\add* on the bank
of the river Arnon, and the city that \add is\add* in the midst of the
river, and all the plain by Medeba;

Heshbon, and all her cities that \add are\add* in the plain;
Dibon, and Bamoth-baal, and Beth-baal-meon,\f + \fr 13.17  \ft Bamoth-baal…: or, the high places of Baal, and house of
Baal-meon\f*

And their coast was Jazer, and all the cities of Gilead, and
half the land of the children of Ammon, unto Aroer that \add is\add*
before Rabbah;

And the name of Hebron before \add was\add* Kirjath-arba;
\add which Arba was\add* a great man among the Anakims. And the land
had rest from war.

And the border of the children of Ephraim according to their
families was \add thus:\add* even the border of their inheritance
on the east side was Ataroth-addar, unto Beth-horon the upper;

And the border went out toward the sea to Michmethah on the north
